.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml:214:  step_fanout_spawn:
.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml:215:    description: "Spawn fan-out lineages; skip and proceed to phase_init normally when single-executor"
.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml:216:    skip_when: "config.fanout is absent"
.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml:218:      Fan-out mode is active. Spawn all lineages. Each lineage runs the full loop in its own
.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml:219:      isolated sub-packet under {artifact_dir}/lineages/{label}/.
.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml:220:      A cli-opencode lineage inside this fan-out is an explicit parallel-detached OpenCode
.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml:221:      session with a separate lineage directory and session id; it is not the single-executor
.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml:222:      self-invocation path. fanout-run.cjs owns the stack-only recursion guard for that
.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml:223:      first-level detached lineage and still blocks recursive same-kind dispatch from inside it.
.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml:224:      fanout-run.cjs owns native and CLI lineage execution; native is run through the
.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml:225:      deep/review command surface with config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir so the LEAF
.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml:228:      After all lineages complete, jump directly to phase_synthesis — skip phase_init and
.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml:229:      phase_main_loop entirely (those are the single-executor path). The merge step in
.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml:230:      phase_synthesis will consolidate results across all lineages.
